  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Number of amphoteric compounds among the following is</p><p>(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BeO</mi></math></p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BaO</mi></math></p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>Sr</mo><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Both compounds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BeO</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Be</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are amphoteric in nature.<br />and both compounds <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BaO</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sr</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>OH</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are basic in nature"
  }
